I think that when a spellbook is identified, the inventory listing
ought to show the spell's level, e.g.

h: a spellbook of force bolt (1)

This would just seem to be consistent.

In fact, perhaps just as priests can recognize blessed/cursed items,
wizards ought to be able to tell the level of an unidentified spell
book (they can get a feel for how complicated the book is by just
skimming it, without studying it).  Wizards ought to have some unique
intrinsic.
